/*

Maximum prefix sum for a given range

You are given an array arr of integers and a list of queries. Each query consists of two indices, leftIndex and rightIndex, defining a range in the array. For each query, calculate the maximum prefix sum within the given range.

A prefix sum is the sum of all elements from the start of the range up to a certain point within the range.

Examples:

Input: arr = [-1, 2, 3, -5], leftIndex = [0, 1], rightIndex = [3, 3]
Output:[4, 5]
Explanation:For the range [0, 3], the prefix sums are [-1, 1, 4, -1]. The maximum is 4. For the range [1, 3], the prefix sums are [2, 5, 0]. The maximum is 5.
Input: arr = [1, -2, 3, 4, -5], leftIndex = [0, 2, 1], rightIndex = [4, 3, 3]
Output: [6, 7, 5]
Explanation: For the range [0, 4], the prefix sums are [1, -1, 2, 6, 1]. The maximum is 6. For the range [2, 3], the prefix sums are [3, 7]. The maximum is 7. For the range [1, 3], the prefix sums are [-2, 1, 5]. The maximum is 5.
Expected Time Complexity: O(arr.size() * queries)
Expected Auxiliary Space: O(1)

*/
// My Code ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

public class maxPrefixSum_Array {

    // now a function to write
    static class  Solution {
        public List<Integer> maxPrefixSum (List<Integer> arr,
                                           List<Integer> leftIndex,
                                           List<Integer> rightIndex) {
            int len = leftIndex.size();

            List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>(len);

            // now write logic to get sum of previous num(prefix ) till current num

            for (int k =0 ;k<len;k++){
                int left =leftIndex.get(k);
                int right=rightIndex.get(k);

                int sum =0;

                int PrefixMax = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

                //logic to add sum in  prefix max
                for(int i =left;i<=right;i++){
                    sum+=arr.get(i);

                    PrefixMax=Math.max(PrefixMax,sum);

                }result.add(PrefixMax);

            }return result;



        }
    }
    //main classs to call
    static void main() {
        
        //testcase input
        List<Integer> arr = Arrays.asList(-1,2,3,-5);
        List<Integer> leftIndex = Arrays.asList(0,1);
        List<Integer> rightIndex = Arrays.asList(3,3);

        //now create obj to give input
        Solution so = new Solution ();

        List<Integer> ans = so.maxPrefixSum(arr,leftIndex,rightIndex);

        //print result
        System.out.println("Your expected output  is : "+ ans + "\n\n Explain :[q1,q2,......qn]" +
                "\nwhere each qi == is a query to get max sum value between those selected index (left,right)");
    }
}
